WEBVTT

00:02.467 --> 00:04.219
KATARA: Water.

00:04.886 --> 00:06.471
Earth.

00:06.763 --> 00:08.681
Fire.

00:09.015 --> 00:10.683
Air.

00:11.059 --> 00:14.521
Long ago the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:14.729 --> 00:18.900
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.484 --> 00:23.363
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:23.571 --> 00:25.532
But when the world needed him most

00:25.615 --> 00:26.950
He vanished.

00:27.367 --> 00:30.912
100 years passed and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.120 --> 00:32.747
an airbender named Aang.

00:33.122 --> 00:35.041
And although his airbending skills
are great,

00:35.166 --> 00:37.752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.961 --> 00:38.962
AANG: Oof.

00:39.045 --> 00:42.298
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:42.590 --> 00:44.342
[ ♪... ]

00:47.845 --> 00:50.223
( MAN READING )

00:50.431 --> 00:54.018
Ever since you joined us, you've been
nothing but selfish and unhelpful.

00:54.102 --> 00:55.103
What?

00:55.311 --> 00:57.105
Look here, sugar queen.

00:57.188 --> 01:00.942
I gave up everything I had so that
I could teach Aang earthbending.

01:01.025 --> 01:04.153
So don't you talk to me
about being selfish.

01:04.362 --> 01:06.322
The Avatar is alive.

01:06.614 --> 01:09.117
I want you to find him, and end him.

01:11.160 --> 01:12.370
SOKKA: This is crazy!

01:12.579 --> 01:14.998
How can we beat a guy
who blows things up with his mind?

01:15.206 --> 01:16.249
AANG: We can't!

01:31.431 --> 01:33.516
( PANTING )

01:33.725 --> 01:36.769
( GRUNTING )

01:36.978 --> 01:38.354
How could you do this to me?

01:38.563 --> 01:40.023
You betrayed me.

01:41.190 --> 01:42.734
You brought this on yourself.

01:43.318 --> 01:44.402
I had no choice.

02:05.381 --> 02:07.592
Okay, I'm ready for some training.

02:26.194 --> 02:27.695
Good job, Twinkle-toes.

02:27.779 --> 02:29.364
Visualize, then attack.

02:30.948 --> 02:32.283
( GROANS )

02:33.117 --> 02:35.370
Maybe you should take
your own advice, Toph.

02:36.245 --> 02:37.246
TOPH: What's the matter?

02:37.330 --> 02:39.457
Can't handle some dirt,
Madam Fussy-britches?

02:44.629 --> 02:47.674
Oh, sorry, did I splash you, mud slug?

02:52.387 --> 02:54.097
( BOTH GRUNTING )

02:54.806 --> 02:56.349
Are we taking a break?

02:58.351 --> 02:59.519
( SCREAMING )

02:59.727 --> 03:00.770
Sneak attack!

03:00.853 --> 03:01.979
( GRUNTS )

03:02.689 --> 03:05.316
Sokka, sneak attacks don't work
if you yell it out loud.

03:07.110 --> 03:08.945
( GRUNTING )

03:09.237 --> 03:10.279
Hungry for a mud pie?

03:10.530 --> 03:12.115
( SPUTTERS )

03:12.740 --> 03:15.243
I'll give you a mud pie.

03:15.868 --> 03:18.746
( GRUNTING )

03:20.832 --> 03:23.376
Uh, guys, I thought we were
supposed to be training me.

03:24.961 --> 03:26.963
Very well, pupil.

03:27.130 --> 03:29.424
I believe we've had enough training
for today.

03:30.258 --> 03:33.886
While Katara cleans up,
let's go have some fun.

03:34.262 --> 03:36.097
- Yes!
- Yeah!

03:37.765 --> 03:39.976
( BIRDS SCREECHING )

03:46.441 --> 03:48.776
SOKKA: Look at all those messenger hawks.

03:48.985 --> 03:51.571
You know, I've been thinking
about getting one for myself.

03:51.654 --> 03:53.448
That way, I wouldn't
have to talk to anyone.

03:53.573 --> 03:55.283
I could just send them messages.

03:55.616 --> 03:58.786
I got to say, I like the idea
of not talking to you.

03:59.495 --> 04:02.373
So, guys, what are we gonna get
with our last silver piece?

04:03.499 --> 04:05.001
We can get more money.

04:06.419 --> 04:07.545
Right there.

04:16.179 --> 04:18.890
TOPH: This is where you seeing people
are at a disadvantage.

04:19.140 --> 04:22.602
Everyone guesses wrong because the dealer
moves the rock at the last minute.

04:23.019 --> 04:25.021
But, I can feel it with my earthbending.

04:30.067 --> 04:31.152
( GASPS )

04:31.402 --> 04:32.737
( CRYING )

04:38.785 --> 04:41.913
You there. Want to play a friendly game?

04:41.996 --> 04:43.581
How could I possibly play?

04:43.998 --> 04:45.416
I'm blind.

04:45.500 --> 04:47.502
You don't have to see to be lucky.

05:13.736 --> 05:14.737
"Flamey-o," Toph.

05:15.029 --> 05:16.906
DEALER: Wow, fancy guessing.

05:17.114 --> 05:19.033
You are amazing at this.

05:19.325 --> 05:21.994
Would you like to make the game
a little more interesting?

05:22.495 --> 05:23.704
More interesting?

05:24.121 --> 05:25.248
How?

05:25.373 --> 05:29.627
Well, let's say you toss in
your friend's fine sword there.

05:29.710 --> 05:34.090
Then I'll put up 20 silver pieces
against it, and that's more interesting.

05:35.216 --> 05:37.134
I'll do it for 40 silver pieces.

05:37.301 --> 05:38.302
( EXCLAIMS )

05:38.553 --> 05:40.596
Forty silver pieces it is.

06:02.201 --> 06:04.537
Sorry, little lady, but...

06:04.620 --> 06:05.663
Huh?

06:05.830 --> 06:06.873
I won!

06:10.877 --> 06:13.462
( LAUGHING )

06:16.883 --> 06:20.261
Where did you guys get
the money to buy all this stuff?

06:20.344 --> 06:21.554
Toph got us money.

06:22.054 --> 06:25.892
She scammed one of those guys in town
who moves shells around all sneaky-like.

06:27.018 --> 06:28.895
She used earthbending to win the game.

06:28.978 --> 06:29.979
Classic.

06:30.062 --> 06:31.606
Ah, so she cheated.

06:32.231 --> 06:34.567
Hey, I only cheated
because he was cheating.

06:34.775 --> 06:36.027
I cheated a cheater.

06:36.360 --> 06:37.486
What's wrong with that?

06:37.862 --> 06:40.656
I'm just saying, this isn't something
we should make a habit of doing.

06:41.073 --> 06:44.201
Why? Because it's fun, and you hate fun?

06:44.577 --> 06:46.287
I don't hate fun.

06:46.662 --> 06:48.706
See? Fun.

06:50.750 --> 06:52.376
( CHATTERS )

06:52.668 --> 06:55.046
Katara, I'll personally make you
an Avatar-promise

06:55.129 --> 06:57.214
that we won't make a habit
of doing these scams.

07:45.304 --> 07:46.305
( STOMPS )

07:47.139 --> 07:48.140
( BELL RINGS )

08:24.802 --> 08:27.471
Guys, I think these scams
have gone far enough.

08:27.555 --> 08:29.849
If you keep doing them,
something bad is gonna happen.

08:29.932 --> 08:33.728
Could you for once stop being
such a sourpuss and just lighten up?

08:34.270 --> 08:35.521
Oh, I'm sorry.

08:35.604 --> 08:37.314
You think I should be more like you?

08:37.523 --> 08:39.025
Like some wild child?

08:39.358 --> 08:40.818
Yeah, maybe.

08:41.027 --> 08:42.862
Maybe then,
you'd see how great we have it.

08:42.945 --> 08:44.113
I mean, look at us.

08:44.196 --> 08:46.574
We're traveling around the world,
making easy money,

08:46.657 --> 08:49.493
having fun, with no parents
to tell us what to do.

08:50.369 --> 08:52.246
Ah, I see...

08:52.329 --> 08:54.331
You're acting like this
because of your parents.

08:54.999 --> 08:57.084
- Whatever.
- They were controlling over you,

08:57.168 --> 09:00.296
so you ran away, and now you act
like your parents don't exist.

09:00.546 --> 09:03.174
You act like you hate them, but you don't.

09:03.424 --> 09:04.675
You just feel guilty.

09:04.884 --> 09:06.010
I do hate them.

09:06.260 --> 09:07.344
I don't think so.

09:07.678 --> 09:09.096
I think you miss them.

09:09.263 --> 09:13.726
But you just don't wanna deal with that,
so instead you act like this crazy person.

09:13.934 --> 09:16.353
Look, I ran away to help Aang.

09:16.604 --> 09:18.272
You know what? It doesn't matter.

09:18.355 --> 09:20.941
These scams put us all at risk,
and we don't need that.

09:21.108 --> 09:23.194
We've already got some
third-eyed freak after us.

09:23.694 --> 09:25.362
Speaking of that third-eyed freak

09:25.571 --> 09:27.448
I think I've come up with a name for him.

09:27.531 --> 09:30.993
What do you think of
"Sparky-sparky Boom Man"?

09:31.702 --> 09:33.079
Just think about it.

09:33.370 --> 09:35.748
We have enough money.
You need to stop this.

09:36.332 --> 09:39.293
I'll stop when I want to stop,
and not when you tell me.

09:46.759 --> 09:48.677
MOMO: ( CHATTERS )

09:48.844 --> 09:50.763
Speaking of money, I'm off to spend some.

09:51.305 --> 09:52.473
See you guys later.

09:58.521 --> 10:00.564
Hawky, welcome to team Avatar.

10:01.190 --> 10:03.109
My name's Sokka, and I'm your new owner,

10:03.192 --> 10:06.570
and as such, I should warn you that
there's already a lemur in our group,

10:06.654 --> 10:08.948
so I don't want to see any fighting.

10:09.031 --> 10:10.074
( SQUAWKS )

10:10.324 --> 10:11.659
( COOING )
Good wittle messenger hawky.

10:11.742 --> 10:13.828
Who's got pretty feathers?

10:14.662 --> 10:15.704
( SQUAWKING )

10:15.913 --> 10:17.123
( GASPS )

10:19.416 --> 10:20.668
( SCREECHES )

10:20.751 --> 10:22.711
You're right, Hawky. This is bad.

10:37.852 --> 10:41.689
Toph, when I was in town, I found
something that you're not gonna like.

10:42.148 --> 10:44.316
Well, it sounds like a sheet of paper,

10:44.400 --> 10:46.819
but I guess you're referring to
what's on the sheet of paper.

10:47.528 --> 10:49.864
It's a wanted poster, of you.

10:50.197 --> 10:51.866
They've nicknamed you "the runaway."

10:52.366 --> 10:54.869
A wanted poster! That's so great.

10:55.578 --> 10:56.704
"The runaway."

10:56.787 --> 10:58.164
I love my new nickname.

10:58.247 --> 10:59.957
Is there a picture of me?
Does it look good?

11:03.878 --> 11:05.671
Well, yeah, actually,
it does look pretty good.

11:05.880 --> 11:07.464
But, Toph, you're missing the point.

11:08.048 --> 11:09.341
Maybe Katara was right.

11:09.550 --> 11:11.552
These scams are drawing
too much attention to us.

11:12.094 --> 11:14.096
Don't be such a worrywart
like your sister.

11:14.430 --> 11:15.556
Think of it this way.

11:15.639 --> 11:18.184
Now you have plenty of money
to help with the invasion plan.

11:19.476 --> 11:20.936
Well, that is true.

11:21.395 --> 11:23.772
I had this idea of making armor for Appa.

11:24.190 --> 11:25.524
( GRUMBLES )

11:26.358 --> 11:29.862
Here's a little extra so you can get
yourself a nice map of the Fire Nation.

11:30.154 --> 11:31.197
You know what?

11:31.322 --> 11:32.489
Make it an atlas.

11:32.698 --> 11:35.284
I do like expensive atlases...

11:35.492 --> 11:39.038
Of course you do, and that's why
this wanted poster

11:39.121 --> 11:41.457
is going to stay our little secret.

11:45.377 --> 11:48.214
Sokka, tell me you didn't buy a bird.

11:48.797 --> 11:51.342
Not just a bird. A messenger bird.

11:51.425 --> 11:54.595
Now we can send messages
all over the world, even to Gran-gran.

11:55.054 --> 11:56.639
Wow, how does it work?

11:57.473 --> 12:00.517
Hmm, uh, I never actually
thought about that.

12:00.809 --> 12:03.771
Hawky, Gran-gran, South Pole.

12:04.355 --> 12:05.564
( SQUAWKS )

12:05.648 --> 12:06.774
I think he gets it.

12:06.982 --> 12:08.275
( SCREECHING )

12:09.109 --> 12:11.195
Hawky, make nice!

12:11.403 --> 12:12.738
Bad Hawky.

12:19.954 --> 12:22.373
Well, look who decided to join us.

12:22.456 --> 12:23.749
Where have you two been?

12:23.832 --> 12:25.251
Off scamming again?

12:25.709 --> 12:26.919
Yes, we were.

12:27.419 --> 12:30.756
And I suppose you don't think
what you're doing is dangerous at all?

12:31.006 --> 12:32.007
No, I don't.

12:32.091 --> 12:33.133
Really?

12:33.217 --> 12:34.510
Yes, really.

12:34.593 --> 12:37.012
Well then, what's this?

12:37.596 --> 12:39.014
I don't know!

12:39.098 --> 12:41.183
I mean, seriously, what's with you people?

12:41.267 --> 12:42.434
I'm blind!

12:42.768 --> 12:44.186
It's a wanted poster of you.

12:44.270 --> 12:45.562
"The runaway."

12:45.771 --> 12:48.524
Is that what you're called now?
Are you proud of this?

12:48.691 --> 12:49.692
Where did you get that?

12:49.775 --> 12:51.568
It doesn't matter where I got it.
The fact is...

12:51.652 --> 12:52.945
You went through my stuff.

12:53.028 --> 12:54.280
You had no right.

12:54.738 --> 12:57.074
Your stuff was messy,
and I was just straightening up,

12:57.157 --> 12:58.742
and I happened to stumble across it.

12:59.159 --> 13:01.829
That's a lie. You're lying, Katara.

13:02.413 --> 13:06.542
Fine, it's a lie, but you've been
so out of control lately,

13:06.625 --> 13:08.043
I knew something was up.

13:08.210 --> 13:10.546
I knew you were hiding something,
and you were.

13:11.088 --> 13:13.841
Don't you walk away from me
while I'm talking to you.

13:14.174 --> 13:15.217
Oh, really, mom?

13:15.467 --> 13:16.552
Or what are you going to do?

13:16.635 --> 13:17.636
Send me to my room?

13:17.761 --> 13:18.846
I wish I could.

13:18.929 --> 13:22.516
Well, you can't, because you're not my mom
and you're not their mom.

13:23.642 --> 13:24.935
I never said I was.

13:25.185 --> 13:27.062
No, but you certainly act like it.

13:27.354 --> 13:30.274
You think it's your job
to boss everyone around, but it's not.

13:30.482 --> 13:32.943
You're just a regular kid
like the rest of us,

13:33.027 --> 13:35.362
so stop acting like you
can tell me what to do.

13:35.487 --> 13:37.281
I can do whatever I want.

13:39.116 --> 13:40.701
I don't act that way.

13:41.035 --> 13:43.120
Sokka, do I act motherly?

13:43.329 --> 13:44.955
Hey, I'm staying out of this one.

13:45.414 --> 13:46.415
What do you think, Aang?

13:46.498 --> 13:47.708
Do I act like a mom?

13:47.791 --> 13:49.418
Well, I...

13:49.501 --> 13:50.961
Stop rubbing your eye
and speak clearly when you talk.

13:51.045 --> 13:52.296
Yes, ma'am.

13:52.546 --> 13:54.423
I can't be around you right now.

13:54.631 --> 13:56.842
Well, I can't be around you.

13:59.303 --> 14:00.846
-( SQUAWKS )
- I know, Hawky.

14:01.055 --> 14:02.389
Why can't they just get along?

14:07.144 --> 14:10.481
Hey, Aang, you want to test out
my messenger hawk with me?

14:10.647 --> 14:11.648
I've got an idea.

14:11.732 --> 14:12.733
Sure.

14:13.317 --> 14:18.113
I'm gonna send a note to Katara and say
it's from Toph, who wants to apologize.

14:18.322 --> 14:20.407
Then everyone will be friends again.

14:20.616 --> 14:24.161
I got to say, Sokka, you continue
to impress me with your ideas.

14:24.370 --> 14:25.621
Eh, it's a gift.

14:28.582 --> 14:30.000
"Dear Katara.

14:30.209 --> 14:32.336
"Sorry for everything.

14:32.419 --> 14:33.754
"Your friend, Toph."

14:41.011 --> 14:42.096
( SQUAWKING )

14:46.058 --> 14:47.935
I know this is from you, Sokka.

14:48.018 --> 14:49.937
Toph can't write.

14:50.020 --> 14:52.481
Ugh! You're all driving me crazy.

14:53.941 --> 14:55.818
I can't believe
we forgot Toph can't write.

14:56.026 --> 14:57.528
Yep, we're idiots.

14:58.237 --> 15:01.448
I guess Plan B is we send a note to Toph
pretending it's from Katara.

15:01.824 --> 15:03.909
I think we're gonna run into
a similar problem...

15:03.992 --> 15:06.036
-( SQUAWKS )
- Sorry, Hawky.

15:06.120 --> 15:07.996
Looks like I'm gonna have
to do this without your help.

15:09.790 --> 15:11.375
Come on, we need to talk.

15:20.843 --> 15:22.344
TOPH: So, let me guess.

15:22.428 --> 15:23.929
You brought me out here
to tell me your sister's

15:24.012 --> 15:26.515
not as annoying as I make her out to be.

15:26.598 --> 15:28.183
Nah, she's pretty much a pain.

15:29.643 --> 15:31.812
She's always got to be right
about everything,

15:31.895 --> 15:34.857
and she gets all bossy,
and involved, and in your business.

15:35.190 --> 15:37.359
TOPH: Yeah, I don't know
how you can deal with it.

15:38.026 --> 15:40.612
SOKKA: Actually, in a way, I rely on it.

15:41.321 --> 15:42.531
TOPH: I don't understand.

15:42.781 --> 15:45.451
When our mom died,
that was the hardest time in my life.

15:45.826 --> 15:50.497
Our family was a mess, but Katara,
she had so much strength.

15:50.706 --> 15:53.834
She stepped up
and took on so much responsibility.

15:54.042 --> 15:56.587
She helped fill the void
that was left by our mom.

15:56.795 --> 15:58.964
I guess I never thought about that.

15:59.506 --> 16:01.216
I'm gonna tell you something crazy.

16:01.425 --> 16:03.343
I never told anyone this before...

16:03.427 --> 16:07.514
But honestly, I'm not sure I can remember
what my mother looked like.

16:08.015 --> 16:11.977
It really seems like, my whole life,
Katara's been the one looking out for me.

16:12.561 --> 16:16.106
She's always been the one that's there,
and now...

16:16.315 --> 16:20.944
When I try to remember my mom,
Katara's is the only face I can picture.

16:21.570 --> 16:25.199
TOPH: The truth is,
sometimes Katara does act motherly,

16:25.449 --> 16:27.159
but that's not always a bad thing.

16:27.576 --> 16:30.787
She's compassionate and kind,
and she actually cares about me.

16:31.497 --> 16:33.957
You know, the real me.

16:34.875 --> 16:36.793
That's more than my own mom.

16:39.046 --> 16:41.215
Don't ever tell her I said any of this.

16:41.548 --> 16:43.008
Hey, my lips are sealed.

16:46.929 --> 16:48.555
( PURRING )

16:51.517 --> 16:53.519
Hi, Toph. Um, I want to...

16:53.602 --> 16:54.770
Katara, stop.

16:54.978 --> 16:56.021
You don't need to apologize.

16:56.104 --> 16:58.023
I was the one being stupid.

16:58.106 --> 17:01.026
These scams are out of control,
and I'm done with them.

17:01.527 --> 17:03.862
Actually, I wasn't going to apologize.

17:04.530 --> 17:07.199
I was gonna say,
I want to pull a scam with you.

17:08.492 --> 17:10.494
What? You want to pull a scam?

17:10.911 --> 17:13.914
Not just any scam. The ultimate scam.

17:14.164 --> 17:16.708
What do you say, Toph? Just me and you.

17:16.917 --> 17:18.168
One last go.

17:18.377 --> 17:19.419
You in?

17:19.503 --> 17:20.921
You know I'm in.

17:21.129 --> 17:23.090
Now what's this idea of yours?

17:23.173 --> 17:24.174
( BOTH GROANING )

17:28.428 --> 17:29.638
The plan is simple.

17:29.721 --> 17:32.307
This wanted poster says
you're worth a lot of money,

17:32.391 --> 17:34.935
ten times more than you've made
in all your scams...

17:35.519 --> 17:38.397
So, I'm gonna turn you in
and collect the reward.

17:38.480 --> 17:41.650
Then you metalbend yourself out of jail,
and we're on our way.

17:41.817 --> 17:43.068
( PANTING )

17:43.151 --> 17:44.861
( GRUNTING )

17:46.280 --> 17:48.031
How could you do this to me?

17:48.323 --> 17:49.700
You betrayed me!

17:50.534 --> 17:52.244
You brought this on yourself.

17:52.578 --> 17:53.745
I had no choice.

18:00.252 --> 18:03.338
You did the right thing
by turning in the runaway.

18:03.422 --> 18:05.507
The right thing is its own reward.

18:05.632 --> 18:07.676
Well, I'm happy to hear you say that.

18:08.802 --> 18:11.388
But... I still want the actual reward.

18:11.722 --> 18:13.140
Of course. Right this way.

18:28.030 --> 18:30.032
Hey, what kind of cell is this?

18:30.574 --> 18:31.742
A wooden one.

18:40.959 --> 18:43.754
That's her. That's the girl
you were looking for.

18:53.347 --> 18:56.183
Do you think this scam of theirs
should be taking this long?

18:56.266 --> 18:58.018
I was just wondering the same thing.

18:58.101 --> 18:59.144
We'd better check it out.

18:59.227 --> 19:01.188
-( SQUAWKING )
- You two behave.

19:01.271 --> 19:02.898
Appa's in charge.

19:03.565 --> 19:04.691
( GRUMBLES )

19:07.110 --> 19:08.654
( BOTH SCREECHING )

19:08.737 --> 19:10.781
( ROARS )

19:13.950 --> 19:15.285
Wait, it's a trap.

19:15.661 --> 19:17.871
Really? No kidding.

19:18.246 --> 19:20.874
Is that why we're sitting
in a wooden cage right now?

19:21.208 --> 19:23.460
Gee, how'd you figure out it was a trap?

19:23.627 --> 19:25.128
Not for us, Katara.

19:25.337 --> 19:26.588
We're the bait.

19:26.797 --> 19:28.173
He wants Aang.

19:28.298 --> 19:29.549
Oh...

19:29.633 --> 19:31.301
I can't believe I was so stupid.

19:31.802 --> 19:34.388
See, this is exactly why
I'm against these scams.

19:34.471 --> 19:35.889
I knew this would happen.

19:36.014 --> 19:38.141
But this was your idea.

19:38.225 --> 19:39.434
I know.

19:39.851 --> 19:42.521
I wanted to show you
that I'm not so motherly.

19:42.729 --> 19:45.607
I wanted to show you
that I can have fun, too.

19:45.982 --> 19:47.943
Katara, you are fun.

19:48.485 --> 19:51.071
If nothing else,
you're at least fun to argue with.

19:51.655 --> 19:54.825
I know your relationship
with your parents is complicated,

19:55.325 --> 19:57.035
and I shouldn't have said what I said.

19:57.244 --> 19:58.245
It's okay.

19:58.704 --> 20:03.041
I was really mad when you said that
because, well, because maybe it's true.

20:03.333 --> 20:08.088
I try not to think about it, but when
I left, I probably really hurt them.

20:08.755 --> 20:10.173
( SNIFFLES )

20:11.675 --> 20:13.343
Where do you think they might be?

20:13.427 --> 20:15.011
Where do you think anyone is?

20:23.729 --> 20:25.063
( INHALES DEEPLY )

20:28.442 --> 20:29.609
Sokka, watch out!

20:29.693 --> 20:30.736
( YELLING )

20:31.027 --> 20:33.530
It's sparky-sparky boom man.

20:33.697 --> 20:36.283
You know, I'm starting to think
that name doesn't quite fit.

20:42.748 --> 20:44.374
( BOTH SCREAM )

20:46.042 --> 20:48.044
-( STRAINING )
- What are we gonna do?

20:48.128 --> 20:50.172
I don't know.
I wish we had some earth or water.

20:50.255 --> 20:51.256
We need bendables.

20:51.965 --> 20:53.216
What about your meteor bracelet?

20:53.383 --> 20:54.384
You could make a saw.

20:54.801 --> 20:56.303
I left it back at camp.

20:56.386 --> 20:58.221
I was worried they would take it.

20:59.181 --> 21:00.390
( SIGHS )

21:08.523 --> 21:10.317
Um, Katara?

21:10.400 --> 21:11.443
Are you okay?

21:11.777 --> 21:12.778
Just fine.

21:12.903 --> 21:14.446
Well, what are you doing?

21:14.529 --> 21:16.740
I'm making my own water.

21:23.330 --> 21:25.415
Katara, you're a genius.

21:25.499 --> 21:27.918
A sweaty, stinky genius.

21:36.802 --> 21:38.428
( GRUNTING )

21:41.473 --> 21:42.808
This guy is too good.

21:42.891 --> 21:44.893
He shoots fire from his brain.

21:45.227 --> 21:47.312
We should split up.
He can't chase us both.

21:59.449 --> 22:01.451
( SCREAMING )

22:04.496 --> 22:05.539
( GRUNTS )

22:14.714 --> 22:15.966
Aang, get up.

22:17.551 --> 22:18.635
TOPH: Let's get out of here.

22:22.097 --> 22:23.306
( GRUNTING )

22:31.982 --> 22:33.608
( GROANING )

22:35.193 --> 22:36.236
( GROWLING )

22:40.740 --> 22:42.158
( GRUNTS )

22:48.248 --> 22:49.374
Hey, I got it.

22:49.457 --> 22:51.042
The perfect name for that guy.

22:51.126 --> 22:52.168
Combustion Man.

22:52.252 --> 22:53.253
Good job, Sokka.

22:53.336 --> 22:55.922
Now let's get out of here
before Combustion Man catches us.

22:56.423 --> 22:58.049
SOKKA: See? It fits so well.

23:02.721 --> 23:04.764
APPA: ( GROWLING )

23:05.807 --> 23:07.267
Well, I'm exhausted.

23:07.517 --> 23:08.894
Hawky, how about you, buddy?

23:09.060 --> 23:11.855
Yeah, you're such a lazy little bird.

23:12.355 --> 23:14.858
Katara, I need your help.

23:17.235 --> 23:18.612
What is it, Toph?

23:18.695 --> 23:20.780
I need you to write
some things down for me.

23:21.114 --> 23:22.991
I want to send a letter to my parents.

23:24.701 --> 23:26.453
I'll be happy to help.

23:38.715 --> 23:40.258
SOKKA: Hey, where'd Hawky go?

23:48.850 --> 23:50.852
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
